<title>USA: Bristol Technology rescinds buyback.</title>
<headline>Bristol Technology rescinds buyback.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bristol Technology Systems Inc said on Wednesday it was rescinding its plan to buy back stock.</p>
<p>The plan, which had been announced April 24, was to have taken place over 20 months.</p>
<p>Bristol, which markets and services retail automation equipment, said in a statement that it was withdrawing the plan to &quot;avoid jeopardising pooling of interests accounting for acquisitions to be made by the company.&quot;</p>
<p>Details of the buyback plan were not immediately available. A company spokesman did not immediately return a telephone call late on Wednesday night.</p>
</text>
